ure victims to the listener."},"1458":{"id":"/docs/armory-1423","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-fertiliser"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/armory-1424","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/armory-1425","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Poisons an existing Office document (currently .docx) with a malicious field code that triggers a WebDAV connection when the document is opened, leaking NetNTLM hashes to a Farmer listener."},"1461":{"id":"/docs/armory-1426","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-forge-cert"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/armory-1427","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/armory-1428","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Forges Active Directory authentication certificates using a stolen CA private key (.pfx or .p12). Implements DPERSIST1 from Certified Pre-Owned. Output .pfx can be used with Rubeus for PKINIT or NT hash recovery."},"1464":{"id":"/docs/armory-1429","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-gmsa-password-reader"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/armory-1430","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/armory-1431","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Reads the msDS-ManagedPassword blob from a Group Managed Service Account (gMSA) via LDAP and parses the values into NTLM hashes for reuse."},"1467":{"id":"/docs/armory-1432","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-god-potato-dotnet"},"1468":{"id":"/docs/armory-1433","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1469":{"id":"/docs/armory-1434","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Privilege escalation from SeImpersonatePrivilege to NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM using a DCOM based Potato technique. Works on Windows Server 2012 through Windows Server 2022 and Windows 8 through Windows 11."},"1470":{"id":"/docs/armory-1435","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-gopher"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/armory-1436","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/armory-1437","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Searches the local workstation for low hanging credential artifacts and useful escalation information. Runs all built in checks with no arguments."},"1473":{"id":"/docs/armory-1438","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-gps-coordinates"},"1474":{"id":"/docs/armory-1439","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/armory-1440","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Tracks system GPS coordinates (within ~1km) if Location Services are enabled. Windows 10+."},"1476":{"id":"/docs/armory-1441","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-group3r"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/armory-1442","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/armory-1443","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Enumerates Active Directory Group Policy settings and identifies exploitable misconfigurations. Queries domain controllers over LDAP, parses GPO files from SYSVOL, and inspects referenced scripts, MSI packages, and other files on shares."},"1479":{"id":"/docs/armory-1444","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-harvest-crop"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/armory-1445","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/armory-1446","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Decrypts AES encrypted Farmer log files written when Farmer output encryption is enabled."},"1482":{"id":"/docs/armory-1447","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-hijack-hunter"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/armory-1448","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/armory-1449","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Parses a PE header to find linked DLLs vulnerable to hijacking with abuse techniques for each."},"1485":{"id":"/docs/armory-1450","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-hook-detector"},"1486":{"id":"/docs/armory-1451","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1487":{"id":"/docs/armory-1452","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Detects hooked Native API functions in the current process, indicating EDR presence. x64 only."},"1488":{"id":"/docs/armory-1453","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-implant-ssp"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/armory-1454","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1490":{"id":"/docs/armory-1455","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Installs a user-supplied SSP DLL on the system for LSA to load on boot. DLL must export SpLsaModeInitialize."},"1491":{"id":"/docs/armory-1456","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-inspect-assembly"},"1492":{"id":"/docs/armory-1457","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1493":{"id":"/docs/armory-1458","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Inspects a .NET assembly's CIL for deserializer calls and .NET remoting usage for privilege escalation triage."},"1494":{"id":"/docs/armory-1459","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-internal-monologue"},"1495":{"id":"/docs/armory-1460","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1496":{"id":"/docs/armory-1461","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Performs the Internal Monologue attack to retrieve NTLM hashes without touching LSASS. Downgrades NetNTLM settings, impersonates non- network logon tokens, and elicits NetNTLMv1 responses via local SSPI interaction with the NTLM authentication package."},"1497":{"id":"/docs/armory-1462","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-junction-folder"},"1498":{"id":"/docs/armory-1463","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1499":{"id":"/docs/armory-1464","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Creates a junction folder in Windows Accessories Startup folder (Vault 7 technique). DLL executed by verclsid.exe."},"1500":{"id":"/docs/armory-1465","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-kee-thief"},"1501":{"id":"/docs/armory-1466","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1502":{"id":"/docs/armory-1467","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Extracts KeePass 2.x key material from memory. Attaches to a running KeePass.exe process using CLR MD, locates KeePassLib.PwDatabase and CompositeKey objects on the heap, and decrypts RtlEncryptMemory-protected key blobs via injected shellcode."},"1503":{"id":"/docs/armory-1468","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-koh"},"1504":{"id":"/docs/armory-1469","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1505":{"id":"/docs/armory-1470","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Koh server that captures user credential material via token/logon session leakage. Monitors logon sessions, negotiates tokens using SSPI, and stores them for later impersonation. Requires SYSTEM context and SeTcbPrivilege for capture operations."},"1506":{"id":"/docs/armory-1471","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-krb-relay-up"},"1507":{"id":"/docs/armory-1472","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1508":{"id":"/docs/armory-1473","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"Wrapper around KrbRelay and Rubeus that automates local privilege escalation in domain environments where LDAP signing is not enforced. Coerces machine account Kerberos auth, relays to LDAP (or ADCS), establishes a control primitive (RBCD, Shadow Credentials, or ADCS), and spawns a SYSTEM service."},"1509":{"id":"/docs/armory-1474","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-ldap-sign-check-dotnet"},"1510":{"id":"/docs/armory-1475","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1511":{"id":"/docs/armory-1476","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":".NET tool that enumerates domain controllers and checks LDAP signing/channel binding settings to assess relay attack risk. Tests both LDAP and LDAPS on each discovered DC."},"1512":{"id":"/docs/armory-1477","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"net-lock-less"},"1513":{"id":"/docs/armory-1478","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text","url":"/docs/armory#catalog","content":"dotnet"},"1514":{"id":"/docs/armory-1479","page_id":"/docs/armory","type":"text