ze the listener easily."},"2212":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-11","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","type":"text","url":"/docs/listeners/file-server#fill-in-the-fields","content":"Type: Select File server"},"2213":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-12","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","type":"text","url":"/docs/listeners/file-server#fill-in-the-fields","content":"Server: Choose the team server where the listener will be created (must be configured beforehand)"},"2214":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-13","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","type":"text","url":"/docs/listeners/file-server#fill-in-the-fields","content":"Port to open: The port that will be used"},"2215":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-14","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","type":"text","url":"/docs/listeners/file-server#click-create","content":"Once it is created, open the File Server workspace from the top bar ( icon) or Tabs > File Server. Select the listener, then use Upload to add files."},"2216":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-15","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","type":"text","url":"/docs/listeners/file-server#ssl-and-certificates","content":"The file server supports HTTPS. Check SSL on the creation form, then configure the certificate in the Certificate section."},"2217":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-16","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","type":"text","url":"/docs/listeners/file-server#ssl-and-certificates","content":"Under Source, choose self signed or manual. Self signed certificates are generated automatically by NukeRat using the openssl command, with the same subject and key options as channel listeners."},"2218":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-17","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","type":"text","url":"/docs/listeners/file-server#ssl-and-certificates","content":"For manual certificates, paste or upload your certificate and private key PEM."},"2219":{"id":"/docs/listeners/file-server-18","page_id":"/docs/listeners/file-server","